title: Two Taps for a Stamp
id: two-taps-for-a-stamp
tab: Post Office · Two Taps
about: Cue has a secret to send. Chip weighs the letter. Tabby gets the message before the letter leaves Cue's hand.
lead: scribe
stage: scribe, chip, tabby
key: F major
meter: 6/8
bpm: 96
backing:
bass: none
finale: "Hush" on 0

tune knock = 0/.5 0/.5 4/1 2/.5 0/.5 | I 3
tune wing = 2/.5 2/.5 5/1 4/.5 2/.5 | IV 3

[the envelope]
scribe: "I wrote one word and folded it small" = 0/.5 2/1 2/.5 4/.5 3/.5 2/.5 1/.5 0/.5 2/1.5 | I 3, VI 3
chip: "Which slot takes a word that weighs this much" = 4/.5 4/.5 2/.5 4/.5 5/1 5/.5 4/.5 2/.5 1/1.5 | II 3, V 3

[postage]
chip: "Two taps for a stamp" = knock
scribe: "One fold for a wing" = wing
tabby: "Pass this note from string to string" = 5/.5 4/.5 2/1 3/.5 2/.5 1/1 0/2 | IV 3, I 3

[the delivery]
tabby: "Mine says hush. Does yours say hush" = 4/.5 2/.5 0/2 4/.5 4/.5 2/.5 0/1.5 | I 3, VI 3
scribe: "How did you read it? It's still in my hand" = 2/.5 3/.5 4/.5 5/.5 4/.5 4/.5 5/.5 4/.5 2/.5 1/1.5 | II 3, V 3
rest 1
tabby: "You sang it" = 4/.5 2/1 0/1.5 | I 3
rest 2
chip: "Next time send the tune" = 0/.5 2/.5 4/1 5/.5 4/.5 | V 3

[repeat postage]

[the reply]
scribe: "Keep the stamp. I'll sing" = 2/.5 2/.5 4/1 1/.5 0/.5 | I 3
  + chip @2: "Hush" = 0/1
